tests/OfficeAgent.Tests/Corpus/** -text
# Within the corpus, the OOXML packages stay byte exact (the rule above), but the JSON and
# Markdown records are text with one line ending on every platform. A manifest written with CRLF
# under -text made every line trailing whitespace to `git diff --check`, and native results are
# bound to the manifest's exact bytes, so its line ending must not depend on the checkout.
tests/OfficeAgent.Tests/Corpus/**/*.json text eol=lf
tests/OfficeAgent.Tests/Corpus/**/*.md text eol=lf

# The agent-selection evaluation is regenerated and compared byte for byte against the
# committed report, for the same reason and with the same failure mode. This was found after
# the corpus rule was added: the first audit looked for SHA-256 comparisons and missed a test
# that compares file bytes directly, so the rule below is scoped by what the files are for
# rather than by how a test happens to check them.
evaluations/** -text
